 $88$ by $9$ using integer division, we notice that\n\n$$\n9<88÷9<10.\n$$\n\nThe quotient $q$ is the left-hand value. So $q=9.$\n\nNext, we find the remainder $r$ by computing $r=a-qn.$ This gives\n\n$$\nr=88-(9)(9)=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write $88=qn+r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}88=\\underbrace{9}_{q}\\cdot 9+\\underbrace{7}_{r}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $q\\cdot r=9\\cdot 7=63.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407744 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "374cafa1-c178-5125-bda0-19b4e1c51892" :knowledge-point/title "The Division Algorithm For Negative Integers"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bd829d3-ee49-5c38-8c08-b6ec51134281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407683} {:answer/id #uuid "5d320045-3505-52c7-9b18-6ee203d791e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407697} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d4c72d-b3a9-5366-9277-17f8104f171a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407713} {:answer/id #uuid "c71f8d3a-2da9-51c9-87c6-9526215b0ec4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407718} {:answer/id #uuid "cdea4221-de0b-5bcf-8afd-ee1233a793b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c71f8d3a-2da9-51c9-87c6-9526215b0ec4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407718} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf6de2b2-e1ba-5267-9188-c2ceca439ab3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 1759218640