 ≡\\,∃a\\in Z,\\,(15∣6a)\\,∧\\,(15∤a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\nTo disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. \nIn other words, we need to show that there exists an integer $a$ such that \n\n$$\n15∣6a\\,\\text{and}\\,15∤a.\n$$\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $a=5$ suffices. \n\nLet's choose $a=5.$\nThen, we have that \n\n$$\n15∣\\underbrace{30}_{6a}\\,\\text{and}\\,15∤\\underbrace{5}_{a}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\nSo, $a=5$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420695 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6414abb9-00d3-55ea-a1e5-da99999c3ccc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary or Sufficient Conditions From Implications"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ca89b64b-5016-52db-ad10-13fc71298748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453656} {:answer/id #uuid "bf064bf2-82e9-5e43-b653-633779214409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca89b64b-5016-52db-ad10-13fc71298748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453656} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a87b594-92ce-5651-a817-9591309b3dd4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454578} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d697a21-38e2-577f-b759-4f3dfc003f64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453658} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a27ab7-0a90-5d43-b7e1-77d9b3615543" :answer