answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "effca90a-310f-559b-9cd6-1949cd3b4c2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453645} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d280a24-a16d-5b3b-963f-bb375f7da8e5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454572} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "005f66ed-8f1a-52f9-827d-2d2e267ad68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453646} {:answer/id #uuid "e960af39-d3a3-5f17-8c2f-2ad92f587599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "005f66ed-8f1a-52f9-827d-2d2e267ad68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453646} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf101830-7404-5e46-b7dd-1e4d16a0cbf7" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5bbf3a4e-b9b9-5f74-9d97-2501c2b02398" :question/math-academy-id "q-183393" :question/problem "$\\,$ If $l$ and $m$ are coplanar and perpendicular lines, then $l\\cap m\\ne ∅.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the implication above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines is a **necessary** condition for $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$\n- **II.** $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines\n- **III.** $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines is a **sufficient** condition for $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$\n- **IV.** $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$ is a **sufficient** condition for $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{(\\,l,m\\text{ are coplanar and perpendicular lines}\\,)}_{\\text{sufficient}}\\,⇒\\,\\underbrace{(\\,l\\cap m\\ne ∅\\,)}_{\\text{necessary}}\n$$\n\nis a true statement. Therefore:\n\n- Statement II is true. $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines\n\n- Statement III is true. $l$ and $m$ being coplanar and perpendicular lines is a **sufficient** condition for $l\\cap m\\ne ∅$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420701 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152076 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6414abb9-00d3-55ea-a1e5-da99999c3ccc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Necessary or Sufficient Conditions From Implications"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd4e79bf-48f6-5054-8a92-7d22fd13b6c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453774} {:answer/id #uuid "55c2d1eb-0dac-55a2-baca-6bb8e8152c96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd4e79bf-48f6-5054-8a92-7d22fd13b6c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453774} :answer-f