ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454577}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb9b0e1b-3e64-5482-b003-6352af7b5cae" :question/math-academy-id "q-183396" :question/problem "$\\,$ If $A⊂B,$ then $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the implication above?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $A⊂B$\n- **II.** $A⊂B$ is a **necessary** condition for $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$\n- **III.** $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A⊂B$\n- **IV.** $A⊂B$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ being true *guarantees* that $N$ must also be true. Therefore, $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- For $S$ to be true, it is *necessary* that $N$ is true. Therefore, $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$ However, note that $N$ being true does *not* guarantee that $S$ is true.\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\underbrace{(\\,A⊂B\\,)}_{\\text{sufficient}}\\,⇒\\,\\underbrace{(\\,A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅\\,)}_{\\text{necessary}}\n$$\n\nis a true statement. Therefore:\n\n- Statement I is true. $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅$ is a **necessary** condition for $A⊂B.$\n\n- Statement IV is true. $A⊂B$ is a **sufficient** condition for $A\\cap \\overset{―}{B}=∅.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421141 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198283 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c26aeaa-9252-5bd3-9ad6-0fc25ca6b03c" :knowledge-point/title "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "177aca68-9ef3-57f2-8782-7922f7