e "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430269} {:answer/id #uuid "6b464259-884f-55c7-b31c-f0287dcea3f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430290} {:answer/id #uuid "81d7ab1d-ae91-597f-a102-075a5920d0b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430297} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a62032-7470-5198-b6ab-1f2fe2d10863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1a62032-7470-5198-b6ab-1f2fe2d10863" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430314} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1ae1a2b-f51f-54d0-b177-a82a21a0fa8d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430356} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d3b3d04-e35f-505f-8628-7f7927d01651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430276} {:answer/id #uuid "b234bb98-5a1b-545d-ada5-467b2dd8155c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430315} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ab8f31-61b0-55ea-ace1-21a1ef7ae4b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430319} {:answer/id #uuid "ed7b269f-953a-54fa-9e61-dd5a4919e14b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8ab8f31-61b0-55ea-ace1-21a1ef7ae4b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430319} :answer-field/id #uuid "e30ad71c-64f9-5534-85f8-dfc05dd3aec9" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2cc63714-8ef0-5462-b695-51b69677adfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-363835" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{5} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$  select the correct options in the computations of the matrix $U$ below.\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce the singular values ${\\sigma }_{1}=2\\sqrt{5}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0.$\n\nNow, we compute the $1$st column of $U.$ It is given by:\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${u}_{1}=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, and we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the second and third columns of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal.\n\nHence, we must find vectors $u=[{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}]^{T}$ such that ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0,$ which is equivalent to \n\n$$\n{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nChoosing ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ as free variables, the general solution is given by:\n\n|  |  | $2{x}_{3}$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-5}} |  |  |\n\nthat we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}={x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the two linearly independent solutions are already mutually orthogonal, we only need to normalize them. Hence, we obtain the second and third columns of $U:$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"40px\">\n                ${u}_{2}=\\,\\,$\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"90px\">\n                {{field-6}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n                {{field-7}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table cellpadding=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"right\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"3\" width=\"40px\">\n                ${u}_{3}=\\,\\,$\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"90px\">\n                {{field-8}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n                {{field-9}}\n              </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $3\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n- $Σ$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,\n\n- $U$ is an orthogonal $3\\times 3$ matrix,\n\n- $V$ is an orthogonal $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=2\\sqrt{5}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0.$\nAlso, the columns ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ of $V$ give us the right singular vectors of $A.$\n\nTherefore, we can compute the first column of $U$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, and we do not have the third singular value, we can't use the same formula to find the second and third columns of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find vectors \n\n$$\nu=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nsuch that ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0$ and $‖u‖=1.$\n\nSolving ${u}_{1}\\cdot u=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}{x}_{1}+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=0,\n$$\n\nwe get the general solution \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}={x}_{2}\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{{b}_{1}}+{x}_{3}\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{b}_{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are free variables.\n\nNotice that the two linearly independent solutions ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ are mutually orthogonal. Therefore, we only need to normalize them. This gives the second and third columns of $U:$   \n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,{u}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the matrix $U$ could be the following:\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157423 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "008e34f8-40a2-54bb-a209-4f32b24572dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2x & 2y \\\\ 2y & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430415} {:answer/id #uuid "47b363cd-6193-5a2d-ba06-aa9a997c8943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2x & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430427} {:answer/id #uuid "c45b8554-38f1-5540-8813-5593409dc832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2x & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430434} {:answer/id #uuid "ce81fb39-4c7c-5dd7-83a4-ded095d5a9e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430435} {:answer/id #uuid "e8fec4ae-162f-5e33-a06a-ab6bd1b856d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47b363cd-6193-5a2d-ba06-aa9a997c8943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2x & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430427} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0ef2dd1-71c9-595b-9973-83cddc9a73a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430442}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89d73552-bd61-5afc-9133-1cbf2f95b120" :question/math-academy-id "q-81008" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}^{2} & -2y\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}^{2} & -2y\\end{bmatrix},$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={x}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-2y.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2})=2x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2y)=0 \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2})=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2y)=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2x & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157425 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "007fcd15-219d-5a7b-979f-5872cbdb9291" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} & \\frac{x}{y} \\\\ \\frac{x}{y} & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430414} {:answer/id #uuid "157d76c9-2e6f-5cdb-897c-847f29e94391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{x}{y} \\\\ \\frac{x}{y} & -\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430417} {:answer/id #uuid "349923f1-1f51-5fc6-9589-ada6acd4c3c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430423} {:answer/id #uuid "7529d158-9818-51d1-bf9e-38fc8f2bbd6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{x}{y} \\\\ \\frac{x}{y} & -\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430429} {:answer/id #uuid "ea727c2d-0baf-5e14-8734-e9b51371b264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} & -\\frac{x}{y}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "349923f1-1f51-5fc6-9589-ada6acd4c3c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430423} :answer-field/id #uuid "eca99a2b-d50a-519b-aef0-e2b86f3c4cf7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "98de8580-5081-5c82-af81-6826d2545a45" :question/math-academy-id "q-102461" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(x,y)$ for the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-y.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-y) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-y)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & \\frac{x}{y}-1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=0\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y}-1)=\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=\\frac{1}{y}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{y}-1)=-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & -\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157425 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ddf99849-1f2b-5c34-828c-164ad4058c92" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "181ea12e-68f7-5d66-9bfc-073d7aa2c4d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430418} {:answer/id #uuid "19ad17a7-e0eb-5580-8a17-cfa45fc556dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430419} {:answer/id #uuid "1ea12d60-f04d-5899-a453-2a3ac7e6a206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430420} {:answer/id #uuid "395ecdd2-b730-5bb3-87f3-ebb7ee1749ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430424} {:answer/id #uuid "c3fb1b6b-cf4b-5080-8f13-4ec357746c3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3fb1b6b-cf4b-5080-8f13-4ec357746c3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430433} :answer-field/id #uuid "df98d6a0-0de7-5458-a3e0-290cebc7112b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a4a0c4af-3f1c-5b85-b0c9-4604955ba8b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-102698" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},1)$ for the function $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the first derivative of $f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},1).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(-\\frac{\\pi }{2},1)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430447 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157423 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c4234a-3aa1-5b6b-b68b-48e6aa2b0dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Second Derivative of a Function Given Its First Derivative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13ee77d7-6a74-593d-8653-f1729b3ea248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430416} {:answer/id #uuid "20928d65-8941-5d29-b370-bfefac08f5a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430421} {:answer/id #uuid "26f5eccf-3c2b-57b9-a065-6eb51f31c8c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430422} {:answer/id #uuid "7bbd3d5c-3ffb-520e-af1f-462296632c8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430430} {:answer/id #uuid "8facc5d4-6498-52b8-8859-3722fd9af6dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26f5eccf-3c2b-57b9-a065-6eb51f31c8c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430422} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dde31b2-4dff-5b09-bd6e-40098b2f0a7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ed948579-cdd5-5155-941d-e802c724684f" :question/math-academy-id "q-163633" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{″}(-1,2)$ for the function $f(x,y)$ given that\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}2xy+{y}^{2} & {x}^{2}+2xy\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since ${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}2xy+{y}^{2} & {x}^{2}+2xy\\end{bmatrix},$ \n we must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2xy+{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={x}^{2}+2xy.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy+{y}^{2})=2y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+2xy)=2x+2y \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy+{y}^{2})=2x+2y\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+2xy)=2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2y & 2x+2y \\\\ 2x+2y & 2x\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate this matrix at $(-1,2).$ This gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(-1,2)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157424 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "037ff08b-3246-5eed-870b-b4951f319c96" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Hessian Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b6147f2-99cb-5e0e-bfe7-1ab9fcb4bfaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430425} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd5f2d0-f063-5f9a-8554-0e38b366ddee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430426} {:answer/id #uuid "4c3b39c3-ebcc-501e-bf32-f62c8ab6fbca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430428} {:answer/id #uuid "9f8b4808-0307-5f43-b835-eaa5d7c78ac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430432} {:answer/id #uuid "e1d3bd0b-8f50-5fda-8e7a-df552a252f05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b6147f2-99cb-5e0e-bfe7-1ab9fcb4bfaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430425} :answer-field/id #uuid "57597420-75c9-5305-b6c7-82cc31ede092" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f2460b1b-0ae3-5791-81e8-e644fac55aa1" :question/math-academy-id "q-102692" :question/problem "Given that \n${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x} & 2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{bmatrix},$ \nevaluate the Hessian determinant of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "For a function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R,$ given by\n\n$$\nf:\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}⟶f({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nthe second derivative of $f$ is given by the $n\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{1}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}^{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{2}∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}_{n}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe Hessian determinant $H(x,y)$ is the determinant of the second derivative:\n\n$$\nH(x)=det({f}^{″}(x))\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since\n${f}^{′}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x} & 2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{bmatrix},$\nwe must have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the second partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x})=-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x})=\\frac{2y}{x}\\, & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(x,y) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} \\\\ \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂y∂x} & \\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{y}^{2}}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} & \\frac{2y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{2y}{x} & 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,1)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nH(1,1)=(-1)\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 2=-4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430655 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147406 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8b307c7-79bc-58de-ab88-b0783857371b" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Answer Is a Whole Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bb73056-9bb2-5c81-af79-24007bd492a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430568} {:answer/id #uuid "41179ec7-a94b-555a-8aaf-935e2fc49a6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430571} {:answer/id #uuid "5c732ae2-b8c2-5cef-81f4-7f6697c28fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430581} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b89e02-de24-5fd0-96c0-932def05e022" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430615} {:answer/id #uuid "dc7e080c-89a9-58ff-ac78-a81f19fb729b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c732ae2-b8c2-5cef-81f4-7f6697c28fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430581} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bee491f-7dd5-5e20-b7cd-84156c8102f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430645}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "27a694ea-4a25-512f-a531-3c15a047f01c" :question/math-academy-id "q-61684" :question/problem "$\\frac{15}{4}\\times \\frac{16}{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "Interpreting the fractions as division, we get\n\n$$\n(15\\,÷\\,4)\\times (16\\,÷\\,3).\n$$\n\n \n\nSince our expression contains multiplication and division only, we can create an equivalent expression by swapping the $÷\\,4$ and $÷\\,3$:\n\n \n\n$$\n(15\\,÷\\,3)\\times (16\\,÷\\,4)\n$$\n\n \n\nInterpreting the divisions as fractions, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{3}\\times \\frac{16}{4}.\n$$\n\nCarrying out the divisions, we arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\underbrace{\\frac{15}{3}}_{5}\\times \\underbrace{\\frac{16}{4}}_{4}=5\\times 4=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430656 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147406 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8b307c7-79bc-58de-ab88-b0783857371b" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Answer Is a Whole Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bff0f413-a5b9-5bdb-a906-8c4ce718f4c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bff0f413-a5b9-5bdb-a906-8c4ce718f4c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430613} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6d2e9ad-b4e5-5278-b6a7-178a56d479ff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "36cbce10-7136-5dc9-8dd6-df6f370a71a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-195616" :question/problem "Expressed as an integer, $\\frac{35}{6}\\times \\frac{18}{7}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Interpreting the fractions as division, we get\n\n$$\n(35\\,÷\\,6)\\times (18\\,÷\\,7).\n$$\n\n \n\nSince our expression contains multiplication and division only, we can create an equivalent expression by swapping the $÷\\,6$ and $÷\\,7$:\n\n$$\n(35\\,÷\\,7)\\times (18\\,÷\\,6)\n$$\n\n \n\nInterpreting the divisions as fractions, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{35}{7}\\times \\frac{18}{6}.\n$$\n\nCarrying out the divisions, we arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\underbrace{\\frac{35}{7}}_{5}\\times \\underbrace{\\frac{18}{6}}_{3}=5\\times 3=15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{35}{6}\\times \\frac{18}{7}=15.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430658 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147406 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8b307c7-79bc-58de-ab88-b0783857371b" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Answer Is a Whole Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7f71153-9c75-5ef3-91b5-ab96482402c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7f71153-9c75-5ef3-91b5-ab96482402c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430604} :answer-field/id #uuid "6098630e-ecf0-5f12-842f-1d3c910f1e8d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4879e2d6-8cad-5506-bb76-0080ddea786f" :question/math-academy-id "q-195609" :question/problem "Expressed as an integer, $\\frac{9}{4}\\times \\frac{8}{3}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Interpreting the fractions as division, we get\n\n$$\n(9\\,÷\\,4)\\times (8\\,÷\\,3).\n$$\n\n \n\nSince our expression contains multiplication and division only, we can create an equivalent expression by swapping the $÷\\,4$ and $÷\\,3$:\n \n\n$$\n(9\\,÷\\,3)\\times (8\\,÷\\,4)\n$$\n\n \n\nInterpreting the divisions as fractions, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{3}\\times \\frac{8}{4}.\n$$\n\nCarrying out the divisions, we arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\underbrace{\\frac{9}{3}}_{3}\\times \\underbrace{\\frac{8}{4}}_{2}=3\\times 2=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{9}{4}\\times \\frac{8}{3}=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430660 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147406 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b8b307c7-79bc-58de-ab88-b0783857371b" :knowledge-point/title "Cases Where the Answer Is a Whole Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18184068-8bbe-5aaa-b472-4c1fdc10006e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430560} {:answer/id #uuid "6df36da5-be2c-5e70-a34b-ddd9550d927d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430586} {:answer/id #uuid "8ac4732d-869a-55af-9d16-3657747a6220" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430595} {:answer/id #uuid "98699e05-5fa7-508d-b75f-cd265da5c7f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430599} {:answer/id #uuid "f8ca717c-ebbc-5f31-b1a9-41aa95fededa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6df36da5-be2c-5e70-a34b-ddd9550d927d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430586} :answer-field/id #uuid "fecac385-daaa-5ecb-995d-e703b50ec88e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident